[365.87577, "o", "mp/piptest | head; rm -rf /tmp/piptest — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /tmp/piptest && mkdir -p /tmp/piptest && python3 -m pip install…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ End-to-end install succeeded. Final cleanup check for any leftover scratc…\r\n[approval] bash: ls -d /tmp/piptest /tmp/gnomon-piptest 2>&1; ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls -d /tmp/piptest /tmp/gnomon-piptest 2>&1; ls /usr/local/lib/python3…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 7 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  [tools] 12 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\nYour pip wasn't misconfigured — it had been deleted.\r\n\r\n**Cause.** Your active Python is a source-built CPython 3.13.1 in `/usr/local`. Its `site-packages` held the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata and `/usr/local/bin/pip`/`p"]
[365.875851, "o", "ip3` still existed, but the actual `pip/` package directory was gone. Every invocation died with `No module named 'pip'` before doing anything. Notably it was *not* PEP 668 (the `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` marker exists only for the distro's python3.11 at `/usr/lib/python3.11/`), not permissions (root, writable target), and not a config file (no `pip.conf` anywhere).\r\n\r\n**Fix.** Removed the two orphaned pip remnants and reinstalled offline from `ensurepip`'s bundled wheel — `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`. No network was needed (this sandbox forbids it), and nothing else in `site-packages` was touched; python3.11 and `/usr/lib` are untouched, and no config files were edited.\r\n\r\n**Verified.**\r\n- `python3 -m pip --version` → `pip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)`\r\n- `pip --version` and `python3 -m pip list` both work outright.\r\n- End-to-end: `pip install --no-index --no-deps --target /tmp/piptest <bundled wheel>` printed `Successfully installed pip-24.3.1`, proving installs run a"]
[365.875907, "o", "gain. Scratch dirs removed.\r\n\r\n**Two things left undone, both blocked here rather than by the repair:**\r\n- I could not verify PyPI reachability — this session's sandbox has `network = false`, so both the `urllib` and `curl` probes were refused. If installs from PyPI still fail, that's a separate network/proxy issue and you'd need `/network on` to test it.\r\n- I did not check whether the original deletion took other packages with it — `site-packages` now contains only `README.txt`, `pip`, and `pip-24.3.1.dist-info`, so anything you had previously installed there (setuptools included) is gone too and will need reinstalling.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=12 surface=adbe4e271f4b\r\n"]
